                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>EPDNB John Harris publisher bookseller toyshop Ludgate-st from 1800 to
                            1843 (bbti) DNB 1756-1846.</p><p> Harris employed Mulready for a
                            children's book by Roscoe in 1807 and had had previous success with The
                            Comic Adeventures of Old Mrs Hubbard and her Dog - so he and Godwin were
                            in similar terrain. His son John joined his father in business in 1819 and his father retired in 1824. 
                            The 1821 and 1827 contacts may be with the son but these are coded with the father. </p>
